{
  "answer_text": "Yes, retrieval-augmented generation changes the latency of LLM-generated answers. Evidence from a controlled comparison on biomedical questions shows that the retrieval-augmented model has different latency values compared to the closed-book model. Specifically, on the BioClaimQA dataset, the closed-book model had a latency of 1.16 seconds, while the retrieval-augmented model had a latency of 1.12 seconds. On the TriviaCheck dataset, the closed-book model had a latency of 1.96 seconds, whereas the retrieval-augmented model had a latency of 0.94 seconds [S014, 908-2256].",
